Intermediate &
Advanced Roles
Each role is marked by a complexity indicator. When playing with less experienced players, you should stick with Basic roles. For more experienced players intermediate and advanced roles can be added. There are also some cards that don't have defined abilities that allow you to customize the game to your wishes.
Basic: The most basic roles that can be used with newer players. Their mechanics are relatively easy for both the players and the Host.
Intermediate: Slightly more advanced roles, that introduce more mechanics such as role changes, day abilities as well as solo roles (see more on that in the following pages).
Advanced: The most complex roles. These might prove challenging for both players and Hosts and should only be used by experienced players.
None: These roles don't have a specific behaivor defined. The Host and players may agree on rules for these roles.